Now that I've won with all of the classes I figured it was time to
start with the races. I won with Elf when it was a class but not until
now as a race.

I didn't have high hopes for this character as I started with only a 13
Int; many of my previous attempts had an Int of 20. But I managed to
max it out eventually, and a wish for a helm of brilliance brought my
Int to 24. I learned 27 spells in total, though the most frequently
used were force bolt, magic missile, identify, and polymorph (I'm a
polypile-addict).

One highlight was when I accidentally sacrificed an elf (that my pet
had killed), thus summoning Yeenoghu. I was getting annoyed with the
demon following me around and was going to leave him near the top of
the dungeon to deal with later. Then I happened to kill a cockatrice
and decided to get rid of him right then and there.

Another highlight: Used charm monster several times on Medusa level. It
was fun to see how many assorted pets I could drag along with me. I
abandoned them all soon, but when I got back to the Castle with the
Amulet a lone Jabberwock was still tame. I brought him all the way up
to the plane of Earth, but he didn't show when I blew my magic whistle
at the portal. I had to put my ring of conflict back on to deal with
the air elementals anyway, so he wouldn't have lasted long.

I played with lots of incubi and nurses to get my HP up to 542 by the
end. I got my AC down to -39 at one point but accidentally lost all my
divine protection by praying in Vlad's Tower. I wasn't in trouble, but
was hoping to get another spellbook. Unfortunately Anhur was displeased
with me. I'm not sure why (and Vlad's Tower isn't considered part of
Gehennom), but it may have been because I accidentally killed too many
friendlies with my magic missile spell. I recovered a few points of my
AC by gathering up gold in Gehennom (>$15K in the Wiz Tower zoo) and
level-teleporting back to the Valley of the Dead to donate to the
priest there, but ended up with an AC of -34: silver dragon scale,
cloak of magic resistance (I didn't trust leaving MR to Magicbane/quest
item), speed boots, gauntlets of dexterity (switched to power in late
game), Hawaiian shirt, helm of brilliance, all enchanted to +4/+5.

I used Magicbane (which was granted to me at +4!! though down to +3
before I genocided R) with Frost Brand as a backup, but mostly the
magic missile spell for the baddies. Juiblex didn't even get a chance
to swallaow me, nor did Pestilence sicken me a single time. Thanks to
the Eye of the Aethiopica I recovered spell points almost instantly,
and even with the Amulet of Yendor didn't have to worry about energy
drain much as I had maxed out at 941 power. I eventually had 0% failure
to cast everything until I switched to gauntlets of power, then only 3%
failure chance. I did use Finger of Death for Rodney which was very
satisfying; only had to kill him six times.

This was not a challenge ascension by any means; I ate everything,
polypiled like crazy, used six wishes, and genocided 34 species. The
only conducts I kept were no polyself (which I very rarely do
intentionally anyway) and no wishing for artifacts (which I almost
never do either). I did die once early on before I got poison
resistance (got too complacent getting that intrinsic at level 3 when I
played Monks), but fortunately had an amulet of life saving. I ended
the game with 3 more AoLSs plus at least 5 potions of full healing.

Final score: 5,468,806. About 100,000 better than my Monk ascension
from a couple of weeks ago, though with both characters I wasn't really
playing for points. I even jettisoned the bell/book/candle this time
and just brought along the gems worth $1000 or more each, so as not to
be burdened in the endgame. I missed getting a screenshot of how many
monsters I killed,  but I think it was on the order of 3800.

